eights of Integers</h1></header><div class=3D"style_problemDescription__T4c=
Pe"><p>The Hamming weight of a number is the <strong>number of set bits</st=
rong> (1-bits) in its binary representation. Given a positive integer <code=
>n</code>, return an <code>array</code> where the <code>ith</code> element =
is the Hamming weight of integer <code>i</code> for all integers from <code=
>0</code> to <code>n</code>.</p><h4 id=3D"example">Example:</h4><pre><code =
class=3D"hljs language-python">Input: n =3D <span class=3D"hljs-number">7</=
span>
Output: [<span class=3D"hljs-number">0</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">=
1</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number"=
