erns/bit-manipulation/hamming-weights-of-integers/image-18-01-4-55GW7SBE.sv=
g" style=3D"color: transparent;"></div></figure>
</li>
<li>
<p>If the LSB of <code>x</code> is 1, the difference in the number of bits =
between <code>x</code> and <code>x &gt;&gt; 1</code> is 1:</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display: flex; justify-content: center=
;"><img alt=3D"Image represents a diagram illustrating a bit manipulation o=
peration, likely within the context of a coding pattern related to bitwise =
operations or data structures.  The diagram shows a binary number, `x`, rep=
resented by three bits: `110` (where the rightmost bit is the least signifi=
cant bit, or LSB, as indicated by a blue arrow pointing to the rightmost '1=
